</script>

# Dialog

A window overlaid on the page with a blurred backdrop. Built on the native `dialog` element with `showModal`, so it renders in the top layer above every ancestor. Clicking the backdrop or pressing Escape closes it, and the panel scales out as the backdrop fades.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Dialog, DialogTrigger, DialogContent } from "#lib/components/ui/dialog/index.js";
</script>

<Dialog>
	<DialogTrigger>Open dialog</DialogTrigger>
	<DialogContent>
		<p>Click the backdrop or press Escape to close.</p>
	</DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/dialog.json
```

## Anatomy

`Dialog` holds the open state and renders the modal `dialog` element while open. `DialogTrigger` opens it and renders a `Button` with its children as the label. `DialogContent` registers its children with `Dialog`, which renders them inside the panel, and its `class` and other attributes go on the panel, such as a fixed width or `style="padding: 0"` for content that fills it edge to edge.

## Trigger

To open the dialog from any other element, pass a `trigger` snippet to `DialogTrigger`. It receives `props` with an `onclick` that opens the dialog. Spread them onto the element, such as a link styled button or a thumbnail.

<Demo section="trigger" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Dialog>
	<DialogTrigger>
		{#snippet trigger({ props })}
			<button type="button" {...props}>Open with a custom trigger</button>
		{/snippet}
	</DialogTrigger>
	<DialogContent>
		<p>The trigger snippet receives the props that open the dialog.</p>
	</DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

## Controlled

Use `bind:open` to open or close the dialog from your own code. The binding updates in both directions, so closing the dialog from the backdrop or Escape sets the variable back to `false`. A trigger is optional.

<Demo section="controlled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Dialog, DialogContent } from "#lib/components/ui/dialog/index.js";
	import { Button } from "#lib/components/ui/button/index.js";

	let isOpen = $state(false);
</script>

<Button variant="outline" onclick={() => (isOpen = true)}>Open from outside</Button>

<Dialog bind:open={isOpen}>
	<DialogContent>
		<p>This dialog has no trigger; a bound variable opens it.</p>
		<Button onclick={() => (isOpen = false)}>Done</Button>
	</DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

## Variant

Set `variant` on `Dialog` to `default`, `secondary`, `outline`, or `ghost` to change the content panel. `ghost` drops the background and border, so content such as an image sits on the blurred backdrop.

<Demo section="variant" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Dialog variant="ghost">
	<DialogTrigger>Open</DialogTrigger>
	<DialogContent>Ghost panel</DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

## Size

Set `size` on `Dialog` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg` to change the content panel's padding and radius. It defaults to `lg`, with 24 pixel padding and a 10 pixel radius like the shadcn dialog, and `xs` also shrinks the text.

<Demo section="size" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Dialog size="lg">
	<DialogTrigger>Open</DialogTrigger>
	<DialogContent>Size lg</DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` on `Dialog` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius, which follows `size` when omitted. `pill` is a true pill and can clip tall content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` for round corners that stay safe.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Dialog rounded="lg">
	<DialogTrigger>Open</DialogTrigger>
	<DialogContent>Rounded lg</DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

## Overrides

The default `DialogTrigger` button takes `variant`, `size`, `rounded`, and `class`, so you can restyle it without a `trigger` snippet.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<DialogTrigger variant="outline" size="sm" rounded="pill">Edit profile</DialogTrigger>
```

## API

`Dialog` extends the native `dialog` attributes, and extra attributes pass through to the dialog.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface TriggerProps {
	/** Label for the default trigger button */
	children?: Snippet;
	/** Custom trigger; spread `props` onto the element that opens the dialog */
	trigger?: Snippet<[{ props: { onclick: () => void } }]>;
	/** Style of the default trigger button; defaults to `default` */
	variant?: ButtonProps["variant"];
	/** Size of the default trigger button, including the square `icon-*` sizes; defaults to `md` */
	size?: ButtonProps["size"];
	/** Corner radius of the default trigger button; follows its size when omitted */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}

interface ContentProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Classes merged onto the panel */
	class?: CompPropsWithChild<"div">["class"];
}

interface Props extends CompProps<"dialog"> {
	/** Whether the dialog is shown; supports `bind:open` */
	open?: boolean;
	/** Visual style of the content panel */
	variant?: "default" | "secondary" | "outline" | "ghost";
	/** Padding, text, and radius of the content panel on the shared scale; defaults to `lg`, like shadcn */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius of the content panel; follows `size` when omitted. `pill` is a true pill that can clip the content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` to stay round */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
	/** The `DialogTrigger` and `DialogContent` parts */
	children: Snippet;
}
```
